From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:54:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tui_gateway: the lineage ledger read sees every row
 of every id, and the gateway reads the legacy leg's parents

Follow-up to PR #2084 review 5889497938 (card t_01a1d47424d2e6ca), three non-blocking nits:

1. No masked row. lineage_ledger_status read each id with _CANONICAL_PENDING_SQL (UNION ALL ... LIMIT 1, no
   ORDER BY), one arbitrary row per id, so a `queued` row inserted before an `unknown` admission on the same id
   answered `queued` and the gateway owned a chat it must not. It now reads every non-terminal row of each id
   (_LINEAGE_PENDING_SQL, the same query without LIMIT 1): any status outside FORWARDABLE_LEDGER_STATES answers
   (sorted, deterministic); else the least forwardable status of the first id in sorted order. The docstring says
   exactly that. RED on 7cd82b40a1: test_an_unknown_beside_a_queued_row_on_one_id_is_never_masked[queued] read
   'queued'.
2. Both directions tested. The tip-queued/root-unknown test is parametrized over the swapped layout (tip
   `unknown`, root `queued`), and each layout also drives the remote-owner pass (kanban_remote_owner._collect,
   gated on _gateway_holds_work): it collects nothing for the chat. A control test shows _collect collects for a
   chat both legs hand to the gateway. These pass on the parent too (both legs already agreed); they pin it.
3. Intermediate compaction parent: fixed, not accepted. The legacy leg reads the chat plus its parent chain
   (session_notifications._session_lineage, 8 hops); the gateway read only {tip, root}. Traced on the parent:
   - `unknown` on the intermediate parent, `queued` on the root: the legacy leg kept the chat and claimed the tui
     row, while the gateway also owned it. Delivery stayed exactly-once only through the per-row durable claim
     (claim_unseen_events_for_sub refuses a row a live other holder has in flight), and the remote-owner pass
     collected for a chat the legacy sweep also served.
   - `queued` only on the intermediate parent: the legacy leg handed the chat back and the gateway claimed
     nothing until that work ended (the "only delays" case the old docstring accepted).
   _gateway_holds_work now expands its ids with kanban_leg_custody.with_parents (the same parent_session_id walk,
   LINEAGE_LIMIT = _session_lineage's default limit, pinned by a test; a read error keeps the given ids), so both
   legs read one lineage. RED on 7cd82b40a1: the intermediate-unknown test saw _gateway_holds_work True, the
   intermediate-queued test admitted nothing.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_kanban_tui_sibling_custody.py (30 passed; 4 fail on the parent),
test_kanban_tui_owner_delivery.py, test_kanban_remote_owner_delivery.py: 69 passed.
